.TH CRETOPASS 1 "2026" "cretopass 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cretopass \- terminal-based secret keeper with vim-style navigation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cretopass
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cretopass
is a terminal user interface (TUI) application for managing secrets.
Secrets are organized as a tree of nodes; each node carries a name, a
description, and optional extra fields (Login, Password, or Custom).
.PP
All data is stored in a single encrypted file of the user's choosing,
protected by a passphrase using age encryption (scrypt key derivation).
There is no cloud service, no network access, and no telemetry. Decryption
happens only in process memory; sensitive buffers are zeroized on release.
Every mutation is auto-saved atomically: the new ciphertext is written to a
temporary file, synced, then renamed over the original path. A transient
.I {file}.bak
copy of the previous version exists only during the write and is removed
once the save succeeds; it survives only if a save is interrupted.
.PP
On startup a settings menu is shown where the user can open an existing
secret file, create a new one, or select from recently used files.
.SH USAGE
The application is controlled entirely by keyboard. The key bindings are
listed below.
.SS "Tree view (normal mode)"
.TP
.BR j " / " k
Move selection down / up.
.TP
.BR h " / " l
Collapse / expand node. On a leaf node, \fBl\fP opens the detail overlay.
.TP
.B Enter
Toggle expansion on a parent node, open detail on a leaf node.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+Enter " / " i
Open the detail overlay for any node.
.TP
.B d d
Cut the selected node (press \fBd\fP twice). The root node cannot be cut.
.TP
.BR p " / " P
Paste the clipboard node as a sibling / as a child of the selected node.
.TP
.B a
Add a sibling after the selected node (falls back to child when the root
is selected).
.TP
.B A
Add a child of the selected node.
.TP
.B /
Start a search. Type the query, \fBEnter\fP to confirm (highlights stay,
navigation is freed), \fBEsc\fP to cancel. While a search is active,
\fBj\fP/\fBk\fP move only between matched nodes.
.TP
.B Esc
Clear search highlights.
.TP
.B H
Return to the settings menu.
.TP
.BR q " / " Ctrl+C
Quit the application.
.SS "Detail overlay"
.TP
.BR j " / " k
Navigate rows (name, description, login, password, custom fields).
.TP
.B Enter
Copy the selected row's data to the system clipboard. A "Copied!" alert is
shown; any key dismisses it. Clipboard targets: \fBwl-copy\fP/\fBxclip\fP/
\fBxsel\fP on Linux, \fBpbcopy\fP on macOS.
.TP
.B i
Edit the node.
.TP
.BR Esc " / " Space
Close the overlay. Password values are displayed masked (\fB*****\fP).
.SS "Add / Edit form"
.TP
.BR Tab " / " Up " / " Down
Switch between fields.
.TP
.B Enter
Save the node. An empty name defaults to "Untitled".
.TP
.B Esc
Cancel. If data was changed, a "Discard changes?" popup appears:
\fBEnter\fP/\fBy\fP discards, \fBn\fP/\fBEsc\fP returns to editing.
.TP
.BR Left " / " Right " / " Home " / " End
Move the cursor within a field.
.TP
.B Enter (on "+ Add Field")
Add an extra field; pick its type from a popup (\fBj\fP/\fBk\fP or
\fB1\fP/\fB2\fP/\fB3\fP to choose, \fBEnter\fP to confirm). Custom fields
prompt for a name first.
.TP
.B Delete (on an extra field)
Delete the field after confirmation (\fBy\fP).
.PP
Password field values display as \fB*****\fP when not focused; the raw
value is shown only while the cursor is inside the field.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <secret file>
The age-encrypted secret file; its location is chosen by the user.
.TP
.I <secret file>.bak
Transient copy of the previous version; exists only during a save, or after
an interrupted one. Encrypted with the same passphrase.
.TP
.I ~/.config/cretopass/recent_files.json
Recently used files list and application settings.
.SH SECURITY NOTES
The passphrase is the only protection for the secret file. There is no
recovery mechanism: if the passphrase is lost, the data cannot be
decrypted. Keep independent backups of the secret file.
.PP
Data copied to the system clipboard may remain readable by other
applications until overwritten.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (a message is printed to stderr).
